# docs/ is INTERNAL BY DEFAULT.
#
# This used to be a deny-list: docs/ was tracked, and each internal file was ignored by name.
# That is backwards for a folder whose whole purpose is internal, and it failed exactly the way
# a deny-list fails — on 2026-09-01 six untracked files were sitting here waiting for a
# `git add -A`, including a 437-line forensic analysis naming a third party as having copied
# the clicker, and a plan carrying unreleased pricing. Nothing had been committed yet, so
# nothing leaked; the next careless stage would have published all of it, to a PUBLIC repo.
#
# So: the folder is ignored, and the genuinely public bits are un-ignored one at a time below.
# Getting it wrong now means a doc is missing from a clone, which someone notices. The other
# way round means a contract or an accusation is on the internet, which nobody notices.
#
# Covers, among others: decisions.md, briefs/, ui-unification.md, ui-migration-handover.md,
# licenses/ (real customer names and purchase references), reference/, openscad-ai-research/,
# and the provenance analyses.
# `docs/**`, not `docs/` — git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation
# under `docs/` can never fire. Excluding the contents instead leaves the directory itself
# visible, which is what makes the exception below work. (Checked: with `docs/` the listing
# files stayed ignored no matter what followed.)
docs/**

# Listing copy is written to be published — it is the text that goes on the MakerWorld page.
!docs/*-listing.md

# External reference clone (unlicensed upstream — reference only, re-clone if missing):
# git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/nelsonjchen/unofficial-makerworld-parametric-model-maker-openscad-docs vendor/pmm-docs
vendor/pmm-docs/

# OpenSCAD render-loop working output (covers/ stays tracked — it is a deliverable)
**/renders/

